From d9d7e6b67dbee9b78c454fc276fba00bb814f5a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: atjiki1 <atjiki1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 22:38:51 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] bt: run a second ANCS client for the secondary device

With CONFIG_BT_MULTI_LINK_EXPERIMENT, show the notifications of the
secondary iOS device next to the phone's:

- ancs.c keeps one client per device. s_ancs_client stays the phone's
  outside the public entry points, which select the client owning the
  characteristic (or the one a timer was armed for) and restore it, so
  the client code itself is unchanged.
- UIDs of the secondary device's notifications get the top bit set, so
  they can't collide with the phone's, and ancs_perform_action() routes
  them back to the right client.
- The secondary client does not touch the phone's session state, the
  disconnected event or the access denied warning, and keeps its own
  post-connection window.
- Once the secondary link is encrypted, gap_le_connect hands it to the
  kernel LE client on KernelMain, which creates the client and runs
  service discovery. Only ANCS is used on that link; service removal
  and invalidation are routed by device.

Assisted-by: LLM
